    "updated_at": "2018-11-21T17:46:54Z",
    "body": "If I can also add one comment here, on Mac OS, Corebluetooth API doesn't provide MAC address. We can infer the information from CoreBluetoothCache entry in /Library/Preferences/com.bluetooth.apple.plist, but the entry is created if device has been connected at least once if I'm right.\r\n\r\nReason being probably that if device uses a \"private resolvable random address\", address will change frequently so that device cannot be used for tracking.",
